    {
      "id": "1026060",
      "title": "",
      "description": "Alternate Service Options:\r\n\u2022 Riders who typically board or disembark at Symphony can instead board or disembark at Northeastern University or Prudential, which are 0.3 miles away (or about a five-minute walk) from Symphony.\r\n\r\n\u2022 Riders are encouraged to instead consider travelling on the Orange Line at Massachusetts Avenue, which is 0.1 miles (or about a three-minute walk) from Symphony.\r\n\r\n\u2022 Riders may also use the Route 39, which operates parallel to the E branch in both directions along Huntington Avenue.\r\n\r\nBackground:\r\nCurrently, there are no step-free pathways from the entrances to the platforms at Symphony, and the station is not able to be accessed by people with wheeled mobility devices. When construction is complete in spring 2029, Symphony will be enhanced with four new accessible elevators, raised platforms for easier boarding, accessible bathrooms, improved wayfinding, more lighting, and upgraded safety features, making the station safer and easier to use for all riders.",
      "severity": 7,
      "route_id": "unknown"
    },
    {
      "id": "1031519",
      "title": "",
      "description": "The elevator will be closed for major equipment upgrades that will significantly improve the long-term reliability of this elevator.\r\n\r\nTo board a Train to Forest Hills: Cross Milk St and go south on Washington St for one-tenth of a mile (two blocks) to the intersection of Washington St and Winter St. Take Downtown Crossing Elevator 892 to the Forest Hills platform. \r\n \r\nTo board a Train to Oak Grove: Cross Milk St and go south on Washington St for 500 ft (one block) to the intersection of Washington St and Franklin St. Take Downtown Crossing Elevator 891 to the Oak Grove platform. \r\n \r\nTo exit the station: Go to the end of the Forest Hills platform and continue down the hallway (follow signs for Oak Grove and Blue Line) to the Wonderland platform. At the Wonderland platform, go to the 53 State St lobby and use State Elevator 975 to exit. \r\n",
      "severity": 3,
      "route_id": "unknown"
